preConditionHook:
// EL: AbsValue(close - open) <= dojiFraction * (high - low).
//
// Brooks's doji, his one-bar trading range: the body measured against the
// bar's OWN range. Not BodyBelowAtrFraction, which measures the same body
// against the N-bar ATR -- a small body on a small bar is a doji here and not
// there, so the two fire on different bars.
//
// Direction-agnostic, so both sides are identical text; the 'body dominates
// its range' and 'never use a doji as the signal bar' sources are this rule
// NEGATED, which is a per-placement toggle rather than a second rule.
// Bar 0 is the signal bar under the corpus convention (it closes, and the
// entry fills at the next bar's open), so the sources that write close[1] need no lag input.
//
// A product, not a quotient: EasyLanguage raises a runtime divide-by-zero
// error on a zero denominator and a zero-range bar is legal data -- such a bar
// has a zero body too and so is a doji at any dojiFraction >= 0.
// One EasyLanguage relational, so el_le.
